WEBVTT

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:11.634
I share my unstoppable curiosity with you.

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:17.410
I'm still able to run through the fog...

00:00:17.429 --> 00:00:21.238
...because I know that you're here for me.

00:00:21.238 --> 00:00:28.885
I guess the shape of happiness is different for everyone...

00:00:28.893 --> 00:00:33.164
...however, I know it's boring when I'm alone...

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:35.050
But, with you...

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:37.160
...it's like a mystery!

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:42.720
It's an enchanting future, where...

00:00:42.884 --> 00:00:47.440
...in order for me to be strong, it's always you...

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:51.820
...that I can continue to depend on, right?

00:00:51.841 --> 00:00:53.421
Just to survive!

00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:55.360
Stumped Q? Don't lose your way!

00:00:55.362 --> 00:00:57.225
Take this moment...

00:00:57.225 --> 00:01:00.820
...to fix your gaze and charge on ahead!

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:03.059
Eternally, we'll always be together...

00:01:03.059 --> 00:01:04.870
...searching and pursuing...

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:08.580
...the meaning of it all.

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:10.710
Truth is nothing but a labyrinth...

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:12.420
...that we try to continue through...

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:16.126
...especially when we are hurt.

00:01:16.126 --> 00:01:18.298
I'll take you, so come this way.

00:01:18.292 --> 00:01:20.133
I'm certain that, on that day...

00:01:20.133 --> 00:01:24.042
...I'll see your smile, face to face!

00:01:39.105 --> 00:01:40.357
This is great!

00:01:40.857 --> 00:01:43.360
Hey Kyuu, Kinta... Let's go!

00:01:44.945 --> 00:01:47.447
Hey, are you sure we have to go diving?

00:01:47.697 --> 00:01:48.573
Of course!

00:01:48.865 --> 00:01:51.743
If you go to the ocean, scuba diving is a must.

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:54.079
The huge, underwater paradise...

00:01:54.412 --> 00:01:55.914
The beauty of the fish...

00:01:56.248 --> 00:01:58.124
...passing by to say hello.

00:02:00.252 --> 00:02:01.503
Isn't that wonderful?

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:03.255
As I thought...

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:05.715
I'm sorry, but...

00:02:06.258 --> 00:02:09.719
I prefer the paradise on the beach instead.

00:02:09.970 --> 00:02:11.096
What did you say?

00:02:11.179 --> 00:02:12.472
N-No, nothing,
N-No, nothing.

00:02:12.764 --> 00:02:14.224
Then, let's go!

00:02:14.391 --> 00:02:15.308
Okay...
Okay...

00:02:25.777 --> 00:02:27.737
That's impossible!

00:02:28.238 --> 00:02:29.739
Please settle down.

00:02:29.948 --> 00:02:33.118
Maybe Ikezoe-san left for home by himself.

00:02:33.201 --> 00:02:36.037
We tried calling his cellphone,
his house, and the hospital...

00:02:36.204 --> 00:02:37.747
...but he's nowhere to be found.

00:02:38.123 --> 00:02:39.291
He must have went diving.

00:02:39.541 --> 00:02:41.042
All his equipment is missing.

00:02:41.376 --> 00:02:43.587
Then, Ikezoe-Sensei is...

00:02:44.629 --> 00:02:46.631
May we check your storage room?

00:02:49.384 --> 00:02:51.428
Um, did something happen?

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:53.471
Well, you see...

00:02:53.555 --> 00:02:55.765
I have a reservation under Minami.

00:02:55.891 --> 00:02:57.392
Oh, welcome.

00:02:57.726 --> 00:02:59.769
Manager, please come with us.

00:02:59.895 --> 00:03:01.021
S-Sure.

00:03:01.313 --> 00:03:03.523
Ah, can you wait a moment please?

00:03:05.942 --> 00:03:06.943
He's missing?

00:03:07.235 --> 00:03:08.069
Yes.

00:03:08.445 --> 00:03:10.572
We traveled here with Ikezoe-Sensei.

00:03:11.156 --> 00:03:14.492
Ah, we were supposed to head
back to the hospital...

00:03:14.826 --> 00:03:17.203
...but he's been missing since last night.

00:03:17.913 --> 00:03:20.665
When we checked for Ikezoe-sensei's
things this morning...

00:03:21.082 --> 00:03:24.336
...his diving suit and equipment were missing.

00:03:25.337 --> 00:03:27.005
What makes you think it was last night?

00:03:27.380 --> 00:03:28.506
It was last night...

00:03:29.007 --> 00:03:31.134
...because we all went out for drinks at a local bar.

00:03:31.801 --> 00:03:35.180
But, no one has seen Ikezoe-Sensei since then.

00:03:35.597 --> 00:03:37.557
There's nothing to suggest he returned to the hotel.

00:03:38.516 --> 00:03:41.561
We all assume he left on an impulse...

00:03:41.686 --> 00:03:44.022
...to go night diving by himself.

00:03:46.566 --> 00:03:47.901
Night diving?

00:03:48.276 --> 00:03:53.365
People do that to observe the fish
and coral in the moonlight.

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:55.283
Just as I thought.

00:03:55.617 --> 00:03:59.412
An oxygen tank and a searchlight were
missing from the storage room.

00:03:59.955 --> 00:04:01.790
A boat is missing too.

00:04:02.791 --> 00:04:05.377
So, that means that Ikezoe-Sensei...

00:04:05.543 --> 00:04:07.253
He probably went diving alone.

00:04:07.545 --> 00:04:08.922
Then, let's search for him!

00:04:09.214 --> 00:04:12.801
If he went night diving, he's most
likely at the shipwreck point.

00:04:13.593 --> 00:04:14.344
It's strange.

00:04:15.553 --> 00:04:17.389
What is strange?

00:04:17.931 --> 00:04:20.141
We all had diving lessons, right?

00:04:21.059 --> 00:04:23.311
Not taking into account that
he dove alone at night...

00:04:23.895 --> 00:04:28.441
...the fact that he was intoxicated is suicidal.

00:04:29.067 --> 00:04:29.776
Yeah.

00:04:29.818 --> 00:04:35.115
So, don't you think it's strange
for an experienced doctor...

00:04:35.573 --> 00:04:37.075
...to do something that dangerous?

00:04:37.283 --> 00:04:38.118
Oh?

00:04:38.827 --> 00:04:43.707
I'm sorry guys, but as you can see,
we have quite a dilemma today.

00:04:43.915 --> 00:04:46.334
Sorry, but we won't allow that.

00:04:46.376 --> 00:04:46.918
Eh?

00:04:47.002 --> 00:04:48.670
Allow us to help in the search.

00:04:48.962 --> 00:04:49.629
Huh?

00:04:49.879 --> 00:04:54.592
Well, we appreciate the offer,
but even if you kids...

00:04:54.884 --> 00:04:56.011
We may just look like kids...

00:04:56.469 --> 00:04:59.139
...but we're all from DDS!

00:04:59.264 --> 00:04:59.764
Eh?

00:05:00.056 --> 00:05:00.640
Eh?

00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:02.100
DDS?

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:06.438
Dan Morihiko's famous DDS?

00:05:06.730 --> 00:05:07.897
Uh huh!

00:05:08.732 --> 00:05:11.151
Geez, he had to flash that...

00:05:16.531 --> 00:05:19.242
Wow, what an amazing luxury cruiser.

00:05:19.659 --> 00:05:21.036
You think so?

00:05:21.411 --> 00:05:24.622
Ikezoe-Sensei owns this cruiser.

00:05:24.998 --> 00:05:26.166
Eh?

00:05:26.291 --> 00:05:29.335
Doctors' sure are rich, huh?

00:05:29.461 --> 00:05:30.128
Yeah.

00:05:30.628 --> 00:05:33.173
Not every doctor is rich.

00:05:34.174 --> 00:05:37.802
Ikezoe-Sensei is, because his
family owns a hospital.

00:05:38.136 --> 00:05:41.556
Hospital researchers like myself, are quite poor.

00:05:41.890 --> 00:05:43.308
Stop complaining.

00:05:43.725 --> 00:05:46.394
We're about to reach the diving point.

00:05:46.895 --> 00:05:47.896
Please get ready.

00:05:48.646 --> 00:05:53.234
The diving area here has a gentle slope.

00:05:53.443 --> 00:05:58.364
About thirty meters down,
there is an old shipwreck.

00:05:59.240 --> 00:06:02.410
If Ikezoe-san went night diving...

00:06:02.702 --> 00:06:04.913
...this is probably where he did it.

00:06:05.205 --> 00:06:07.290
Search around this area, please...

00:06:07.415 --> 00:06:09.084
...and focus on the shipwreck.

00:06:09.584 --> 00:06:11.419
Alright, let's go!

00:06:11.795 --> 00:06:12.462
Okay.

00:06:12.837 --> 00:06:13.505
Huh?

00:06:14.130 --> 00:06:15.548
What are you doing, Kyuu?

00:06:16.466 --> 00:06:18.510
Are you trying to get out of diving?

00:06:18.551 --> 00:06:21.054
Eh? Well, you see...

00:06:21.179 --> 00:06:25.600
Come to think of it, Kyuu, when
we had diving lessons at DDS...

00:06:25.934 --> 00:06:27.977
...you always had a stomach ache, didn't you?

00:06:28.895 --> 00:06:31.106
1
Kyuu, it's just diving...

00:06:31.147 --> 00:06:32.607
...so you don't need to know how to swim.

00:06:33.108 --> 00:06:33.900
But...

00:06:34.067 --> 00:06:36.152
Ah, you're too much trouble.

00:06:36.653 --> 00:06:40.365
I-I'm fine! Please, just leave me here!

00:06:40.365 --> 00:06:41.116
It's okay,

00:06:41.116 --> 00:06:43.243
Diving and swimming are different.

00:06:43.243 --> 00:06:44.828
It doesn't matter what you say!

00:06:44.911 --> 00:06:47.288
I'm not good with water!

00:06:47.539 --> 00:06:50.375
Hey, hey, you have a beginner with you?

00:06:50.708 --> 00:06:52.377
Are you going to be okay?

00:06:52.544 --> 00:06:54.379
No, I'm not okay!

00:06:55.130 --> 00:06:57.465
You should have more confidence than that.

00:06:57.674 --> 00:06:58.842
If there's beginners here...

00:06:58.925 --> 00:07:00.969
...I suggest we use a buddy system.

00:07:01.928 --> 00:07:02.804
Buddy?

00:07:02.971 --> 00:07:04.222
Buddy system...

00:07:04.806 --> 00:07:06.850
It's when you dive in pairs.

00:07:07.433 --> 00:07:08.393
That's right!

00:07:08.685 --> 00:07:11.104
With an expert helping you, you'll
have nothing to worry about.

00:07:11.646 --> 00:07:12.772
III dive with Kyuu.

00:07:13.231 --> 00:07:14.858
Kinta, you stay with Kazuma.

00:07:15.233 --> 00:07:15.900
Okay.

00:07:16.151 --> 00:07:17.694
I'll be fine on my own.

00:07:18.194 --> 00:07:20.613
Despite my looks, I'm good at diving.

00:07:20.822 --> 00:07:22.448
Everything's been decided, right?

00:07:22.824 --> 00:07:24.325
I guess...

00:07:30.665 --> 00:07:32.250
Hurry up and get in!

00:07:35.837 --> 00:07:37.922
W-Would it be all right to stay here?

00:07:38.089 --> 00:07:39.424
Hurry up and get in!

00:07:43.386 --> 00:07:44.429
Help!

00:07:46.389 --> 00:07:47.348
Hold on to me.

00:07:48.474 --> 00:07:49.225
Are you okay?

00:07:50.268 --> 00:07:51.102
Yeah.

00:07:51.603 --> 00:07:52.812
That's just like Ryu-kun.

00:08:27.972 --> 00:08:29.265
<i>Eh?</i>

00:08:29.974 --> 00:08:32.268
<i>I guess I don’t need to know how to swim.</i>

00:08:33.561 --> 00:08:38.358
<i>That’s good, since the ocean
down here is so beautiful</i>

00:09:07.595 --> 00:09:08.471
<i>That’s it, right?</i>

00:10:35.433 --> 00:10:36.476
Are you all right, Megu?

00:10:37.060 --> 00:10:37.769
Yeah.

00:10:38.269 --> 00:10:39.437
What happened?

00:10:39.896 --> 00:10:42.065
I was attacked.

00:10:42.357 --> 00:10:43.483
What?
What?

00:11:09.092 --> 00:11:09.675
<i>Huh?</i>

00:11:10.843 --> 00:11:12.553
<i>The tank is empty?</i>

00:12:18.870 --> 00:12:19.704
Are you all right?

00:12:20.455 --> 00:12:21.956
Yeah, thank you.

00:12:22.832 --> 00:12:24.292
Hyperventilation...

00:12:25.668 --> 00:12:28.504
It happens to many beginners like yourself.

00:12:29.505 --> 00:12:34.510
Without even noticing, you use up
more oxygen than you require.

00:12:35.178 --> 00:12:36.053
Eh?

00:12:36.554 --> 00:12:38.681
Anyway, I'm glad you're all right.

00:12:40.224 --> 00:12:43.269
Yes, in the shipwreck. Yes.

00:12:43.728 --> 00:12:44.604
His name?

00:12:44.854 --> 00:12:47.982
It was... Ikezoe Hajime, one of my customers.

00:12:48.983 --> 00:12:50.234
From our examination...

00:12:50.485 --> 00:12:53.946
...the victim died from a head fracture.

00:12:54.864 --> 00:12:57.909
We also found alcohol in his blood.

00:12:58.618 --> 00:13:02.121
We estimate that the time of
death was late last night.

00:13:02.371 --> 00:13:08.336
Most likely, he went night diving by himself
and was trapped in that room.

00:13:08.753 --> 00:13:14.550
In a panic, he hit his head, and died soon after.

00:13:15.676 --> 00:13:18.429
Because it wa a locked cabin...

00:13:19.055 --> 00:13:21.557
...there's not much chance
that someone else did this.

00:13:22.391 --> 00:13:23.851
Is that true?

00:13:24.060 --> 00:13:24.769
What?

00:13:24.894 --> 00:13:26.646
Are you saying it's not an accident?

00:13:30.149 --> 00:13:33.861
Ridiculous! How could it be something
other than an accident?

00:13:34.779 --> 00:13:37.448
How do you explain Megu being attacked?

00:13:41.577 --> 00:13:44.288
Perhaps someone was playing a prank?

00:13:44.539 --> 00:13:45.456
A prank?

00:13:46.165 --> 00:13:50.753
Who would play a prank that could take
someone's life if something unexpected happened?

00:13:52.630 --> 00:13:53.756
You're right.

00:13:54.090 --> 00:13:54.882
I'm sorry.

00:13:55.633 --> 00:13:57.343
Let's head back to shore.

00:13:57.927 --> 00:13:59.804
We need to report this to the police.

00:14:04.517 --> 00:14:05.226
Hmm...

00:14:07.103 --> 00:14:08.062
What is it?

00:14:08.312 --> 00:14:12.483
If the situation is how Kawakita-san
explained, then in the room...

00:14:19.657 --> 00:14:20.533
I see!

00:14:21.033 --> 00:14:22.410
That's very odd!

00:14:22.618 --> 00:14:23.160
Eh?

00:14:23.327 --> 00:14:25.162
What's odd, Kyuu?

00:14:25.413 --> 00:14:28.374
But, if so, then who...

00:14:28.874 --> 00:14:31.335
Ah, I have no idea what you are saying!

00:14:31.794 --> 00:14:34.338
We didn't have the chance to see the cabin.

00:14:34.922 --> 00:14:35.923
Hey Ryu-kun...

00:14:36.424 --> 00:14:41.762
...is it true that the deeper you dive,
the more oxygen you use?

00:14:42.054 --> 00:14:43.556
Yes, that's right.

00:14:44.098 --> 00:14:47.268
The deeper you dive, the more oxygen you use.

00:14:48.894 --> 00:14:49.979
Hey, Kyuu!

00:14:51.814 --> 00:14:52.398
I see!

00:14:52.940 --> 00:14:54.066
So, that's what he's thinking!

00:14:54.650 --> 00:14:55.443
Huh?

00:15:06.245 --> 00:15:07.538
A first aid kit?

00:15:08.039 --> 00:15:11.292
Yes, one of my friends has cut their finger.

00:15:11.792 --> 00:15:13.044
Hold on a second.

00:15:13.711 --> 00:15:14.462
Megu!

00:15:15.212 --> 00:15:16.672
Ah, there he is.

00:15:17.840 --> 00:15:19.300
Please recall something for me.

00:15:22.386 --> 00:15:23.179
That's what I thought.

00:15:23.804 --> 00:15:25.389
Which means...

00:15:27.099 --> 00:15:27.975
There's no mistake.

00:15:29.060 --> 00:15:31.896
But, what about the locked cabin?

00:15:32.438 --> 00:15:33.564
It's also a trick.

00:15:34.315 --> 00:15:35.107
Ryu-kun?

00:15:35.858 --> 00:15:39.570
It's easy to create a locked
room in this scenario.

00:15:42.899 --> 00:15:44.066
The mystery is solved.
The mystery is solved.

00:15:51.199 --> 00:15:52.700
A murder case?

00:15:53.117 --> 00:15:54.202
What do you mean?

00:15:54.327 --> 00:15:56.162
Impossible! This was an accident

00:15:56.329 --> 00:16:00.249
No. I'm sorry, but this is definitely a murder.

00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:03.669
Please remember what we saw in the cabin.

00:16:10.051 --> 00:16:13.262
When I checked Ikezoe-san in the cabin...

00:16:13.638 --> 00:16:15.681
...I saw the gauge on his tank.

00:16:16.682 --> 00:16:18.768
Ikezoe-san's tank was empty.

00:16:19.810 --> 00:16:21.020
Isn't it odd that an experienced diver...

00:16:21.103 --> 00:16:24.941
...would use a full tank for a thirty meter dive?

00:16:25.566 --> 00:16:28.819
The actual cause of death
was probably suffocation.

00:16:29.570 --> 00:16:32.865
Maybe the air regulator was faulty.

00:16:34.033 --> 00:16:37.411
Then, that leaked air would accumulate
at the top of the cabin.

00:16:38.412 --> 00:16:41.040
But, that wasn't the case.

00:16:42.583 --> 00:16:46.045
That means the victim did not die in that cabin.

00:16:46.796 --> 00:16:48.631
He was murdered...

00:16:48.839 --> 00:16:49.840
...then moved there at a later time.

00:16:50.007 --> 00:16:52.843
But the cabin was locked, right?

00:16:53.302 --> 00:16:54.011
Yes.

00:16:54.512 --> 00:16:57.348
It's true that the door was indeed locked.

00:16:58.182 --> 00:17:02.019
But, it's possible to lock that
door from the outside.

00:17:02.395 --> 00:17:03.229
What?

00:17:03.854 --> 00:17:08.526
The ocean had corroded the door,
and there were many gaps, so...

00:17:09.318 --> 00:17:12.613
...with a small trick, the door could
be locked from the outside...

00:17:14.615 --> 00:17:15.783
...using this.

00:17:16.242 --> 00:17:17.118
What is that?

00:17:17.952 --> 00:17:21.539
This is surgical fiber from the first aid kit.

00:17:22.873 --> 00:17:24.250
Before closing the door...

00:17:24.959 --> 00:17:28.587
...you tie the string to the lock...

00:17:30.798 --> 00:17:35.928
...then by pulling on it slowly, the door will lock.

00:17:36.554 --> 00:17:39.307
I thought you would be better, but
that's just childish reasoning.

00:17:40.182 --> 00:17:42.560
That string would be there
if the door was locked...

00:17:43.185 --> 00:17:45.604
...but there wasn't any string there.

00:17:45.980 --> 00:17:48.816
As doctors you should know that...

00:17:49.567 --> 00:17:53.070
...in time, this surgical fiber dissolves in water.

00:17:53.237 --> 00:17:53.988
Eh?

00:17:54.488 --> 00:17:57.992
With a water-soluble string, there would
be no remnants at the crime scene.

00:17:58.868 --> 00:18:00.619
That really exists?

00:18:00.995 --> 00:18:03.205
Sorry, but that's also impossible.

00:18:03.539 --> 00:18:07.793
There's no way it would dissolve
in just thirty minutes.

00:18:10.338 --> 00:18:11.088
Ryu-kun...

00:18:13.215 --> 00:18:16.135
Well, I guess their theory is impossible.

00:18:16.427 --> 00:18:19.388
The name DDS doesn't mean anything, huh?

00:18:20.765 --> 00:18:21.766
Please wait a moment!

00:18:22.350 --> 00:18:25.394
I'd like everyone to remember the situation...

00:18:25.978 --> 00:18:28.522
...when we dove to search for Ikezoe-san.

00:18:29.523 --> 00:18:31.025
As a beginner, I paired with Ryu-kun...

00:18:31.525 --> 00:18:34.153
...and Kazuma and Kinta we're also paired.

00:18:34.528 --> 00:18:35.696
Megu dove alone.

00:18:36.155 --> 00:18:44.997
I remember seeing three solo
divers and a pair pass by me.

00:18:45.498 --> 00:18:47.625
Eh? But, that means...

00:18:47.666 --> 00:18:48.376
Yes.

00:18:48.834 --> 00:18:51.504
There were a total of ten people that dove.

00:18:52.046 --> 00:18:53.714
Megu's photographic memory is recognized...

00:18:54.048 --> 00:18:57.259
...by the National Institute
of Ability Development...

00:18:57.468 --> 00:18:58.469
...so we can trust it.

00:18:59.053 --> 00:19:00.554
Ten...

00:19:01.889 --> 00:19:04.266
There was someone else besides us?

00:19:04.767 --> 00:19:08.354
That explains why she was attacked.

00:19:08.896 --> 00:19:10.314
ls that so?

00:19:10.940 --> 00:19:15.903
There was a way to have ten people
without needing another person.

00:19:17.279 --> 00:19:17.947
<i>Yes.</i>

00:19:18.572 --> 00:19:24.078
It's a daring trick that takes advantage
of the ocean environment.

00:19:26.539 --> 00:19:30.000
The perpetrator dressed the
victim in a diving suit...

00:19:30.292 --> 00:19:32.837
...and submerged him in
the water, tied to a rope.

00:19:33.838 --> 00:19:39.552
Then, the body was moved along with the
boat to the diving point the next day.

00:19:40.678 --> 00:19:46.350
While we were distracted, the perpetrator
went unnoticed, and cut the rope.

00:19:47.726 --> 00:19:51.439
Swimming innocently, he dove
right along side of us...

00:19:52.690 --> 00:19:56.193
...making the victim look like his partner.

00:19:57.903 --> 00:20:01.824
It's a trick that used the ocean...

00:20:02.533 --> 00:20:09.373
...the restrictive view front the goggles,
and indistinct diving suits.

00:20:11.876 --> 00:20:15.045
Then, who is the perpetrator?

00:20:16.005 --> 00:20:19.175
Someone suggested that we use
the buddy system, right?

00:20:23.554 --> 00:20:25.014
Huh? Me?

00:20:25.723 --> 00:20:29.602
Ikezoe-san's murderer is none
other than you, Akiyama-san.

00:20:30.478 --> 00:20:32.146
W-What are you saying?

00:20:32.438 --> 00:20:36.775
The buddy system suggestion
makes me suspicious?

00:20:37.151 --> 00:20:40.654
Either way, there's no evidence
to suggest it's me.

00:20:41.280 --> 00:20:42.406
There is evidence.

00:20:42.531 --> 00:20:43.282
Eh?

00:20:45.659 --> 00:20:46.410
It's this.

00:20:48.454 --> 00:20:50.039
Again with the tank?

00:20:50.581 --> 00:20:55.711
After checking everyone's tank, there's
one similar to mine and the victim's.

00:20:58.088 --> 00:21:01.550
Akiyama-san, this is your gauge, right?

00:21:02.510 --> 00:21:05.513
This tank is almost empty.

00:21:06.430 --> 00:21:07.723
How could an expert such as yourself...

00:21:08.140 --> 00:21:11.769
Use the same amount of oxygen that I did?

00:21:12.269 --> 00:21:13.229
I see!

00:21:13.354 --> 00:21:14.563
So, that's the answer!

00:21:14.688 --> 00:21:15.231
Huh?

00:21:15.481 --> 00:21:18.317
Oxygen use is directly related to depth.

00:21:18.859 --> 00:21:22.821
So, the deeper you dive, the
more oxygen you use.

00:21:24.281 --> 00:21:25.157
That's correct.

00:21:25.991 --> 00:21:29.662
The perpetrator had to dive
to the shipwreck quickly...

00:21:30.079 --> 00:21:32.540
...in order to prepare the locked cabin.

00:21:33.541 --> 00:21:34.792
When you're at that depth...

00:21:35.251 --> 00:21:40.464
...you use more oxygen than everyone else.

00:21:41.549 --> 00:21:47.221
I learned about hyperventilation from Ryu-kun and I noticed it.

00:21:48.347 --> 00:21:49.682
Akiyama-Sensei...

00:21:50.224 --> 00:21:52.059
There's no way...

00:21:52.601 --> 00:21:56.355
W-What? That's just speculation.

00:21:56.522 --> 00:21:57.773
Why...

00:21:57.856 --> 00:22:03.821
Akiyama-san, earlier you said the line wouldn't
dissolve in thirty minutes, right?

00:22:04.154 --> 00:22:04.905
What?

00:22:05.281 --> 00:22:08.325
How did you know how long it would take?

00:22:08.450 --> 00:22:09.243
Ah!

00:22:09.827 --> 00:22:14.123
We never said anything about how
long the preparation took.

00:22:15.082 --> 00:22:21.213
Akiyarna-san, that is the evidence
that you are the murderer.

00:22:21.880 --> 00:22:23.299
In this situation...

00:22:23.882 --> 00:22:27.553
...you could have doubled the string
and removed it completely.

00:22:28.971 --> 00:22:32.141
There was never a reason to use a water
soluble material in the first place.

00:22:33.058 --> 00:22:34.935
You used that as bait, eh?

00:22:35.853 --> 00:22:38.814
That's all there is to it, Akiyama-san.

00:22:42.401 --> 00:22:44.903
I can't believe you kids saw through that.

00:22:45.904 --> 00:22:47.865
Akiyama, you!

00:22:48.657 --> 00:22:50.200
Why did you do that?

00:22:50.951 --> 00:22:53.662
Because he was the hospital director's son.

00:22:54.413 --> 00:22:57.249
The director wouldn't recognize my skills...

00:22:57.458 --> 00:22:59.627
...even though I was more talented than his son.

00:23:00.127 --> 00:23:03.047
He promised his son the future.

00:23:03.505 --> 00:23:05.549
How can I forgive that injustice?

00:23:06.467 --> 00:23:07.509
But, still...

00:23:07.968 --> 00:23:13.057
I just want to see that arrogant director suffer.

00:23:13.474 --> 00:23:14.683
That's horrible...

00:23:15.684 --> 00:23:19.605
Had it not been for you guys, everything
would have been fine.

00:23:37.289 --> 00:23:40.466
The Sun is setting in a red glow...

00:23:41.057 --> 00:23:43.598
...as it follows me.

00:23:43.955 --> 00:23:46.723
Along this deserted beach...

00:23:46.723 --> 00:23:50.693
...I walk alone once more.

00:23:50.706 --> 00:23:54.075
I can't continue to hold in...

00:23:54.697 --> 00:23:57.090
...the tears that should pour out.

00:23:57.738 --> 00:24:00.167
Why have these memories...

00:24:00.169 --> 00:24:03.699
...become so wonderful?

00:24:04.270 --> 00:24:09.266
Ah... Like an ocean wave, I return to you...

00:24:09.516 --> 00:24:12.039
...because I'm so in love.

00:24:12.772 --> 00:24:15.757
And, now my heart...

00:24:15.757 --> 00:24:17.900
...is heavy with pain.

00:24:18.854 --> 00:24:21.794
Reflections of a bright rainbow...

00:24:21.928 --> 00:24:26.057
...shine on the distant shores of yesterday.

00:24:26.408 --> 00:24:30.028
I'll never forget those days...

00:24:30.035 --> 00:24:35.121
...and I long to see you again.

00:24:38.885 --> 00:24:42.013
DDS is faced with a human disappearing act!

00:24:43.515 --> 00:24:45.267
It's a challenge between A Class and Q Class.

00:24:46.518 --> 00:24:48.895
Hmm, was this really a disappearance?

00:24:50.146 --> 00:24:52.232
Solve the Case of the Disappearance in Thin Air!

00:24:53.275 --> 00:24:54.609
There's only one answer!

00:24:56.945 --> 00:24:58.363
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:24:59.489 --> 00:25:00.573
Wow!

00:25:00.740 --> 00:25:03.159
Wait, you don't have to...

00:25:03.159 --> 00:25:03.910
There!

00:25:03.910 --> 00:25:04.953
Sensei!

00:25:05.745 --> 00:25:07.414
Katagiri-Sensei!
Katagiri-Sensei!

00:25:07.831 --> 00:25:09.541
She's gorgeous!
